; bench.bl — one kernel, eight entry paths, measured from beam-lisp.
;
; WHAT THIS IS. `invm.bench/run` is handed the resident port executable and the
; text IR the generated kernel was compiled from, and answers one question: for
; the SAME compiled kernel and the SAME fixtures, what does an entry cost
; through each supported door —
;
;   :rt          fusion.pipeline/rt-run        — the shipped runtime, written as
;                                                a user would (binary->list
;                                                inside the timed body).
;   :beam        fusion.pipeline/fused-run     — the generated Core loop,
;                                                Elixir.Krt.FusedPipeline.run/2.
;   :port        fusion.driver/native-request! — the resident j1_probe sidecar,
;                                                one framed roundtrip per call.
;   :nif         fusion.invm/kernel-call       — the in-VM regular-scheduler NIF
;                                                entry. ADMITTED ONLY <= 4096
;                                                bytes (see THE MATRIX below).
;   :nif-dirty   fusion.invm/kernel-call-dirty — the same resource through the
;                                                dirty-CPU entry, 0..1 MiB.
;   :noop        fusion.invm/kernel-noop       — regular entry that validates
;                                                and returns `init` untouched:
;                                                the entry's own overhead.
;   :noop-dirty  fusion.invm/kernel-noop-dirty — the same on the dirty entry.
;   :bl-noop     this file's `bl-noop`         — a pure BL function returning
;                                                `init`: the harness floor. A
;                                                door that is not cheaper than
;                                                this is measuring the wrapper.
;
; Every variant is handed the SAME binary and the SAME initial accumulator, and
; every returned value is asserted against fusion.fixtures' oracle — except the
; three no-op variants, whose kernel output is different BY CONSTRUCTION: their
; expected value is the INITIAL accumulator, not the fold's result. A run that
; compares a no-op against the fold would fail; that is the point of recording
; the two expectations separately.
;
; THE MATRIX — regular NIF > 4096 bytes is a POLICY REFUSAL, NOT A TIMING.
; The regular entry admits at most REGULAR-CAP bytes (the NIF's own contract).
; For the four ladder sizes above it the matrix records
;   {:policy :refused-regular-cap-4096 :timing nil}
; and there is NO sample — a zero there would be a fabricated measurement of a
; call the entry is not allowed to make. `refusal-rows` then proves the refusal
; is real by calling the regular entry with 4097 bytes and requiring it to throw.
;
; REUSE, NOT A SECOND FRAMEWORK. The port protocol (spawn/READY/one framed
; roundtrip) and the input contract come from fusion.driver — `spawn-fold!`,
; `await-ready!`, `native-request!` — which is loaded before this file. Its
; measure loop is not reused because it is closed over its own three-variant
; dispatch (`call-adapter`); widening it would mean editing driver.bl, which the
; task forbids, and would give two code paths for one sample shape.
;
; NO CONVERSION ON THE NATIVE PATH. The binary is handed to kernel-call /
; kernel-call-dirty / the no-ops exactly as it is: Rustler's Binary borrows the
; existing BEAM binary, so there is no per-call descriptor lookup (the resource
; is compiled ONCE for the whole warm matrix) and no binary->list conversion.
; The `:rt` variant is the one that converts, and its adapter cost is inside its
; own number, as published.
;
; WHAT THIS DOES NOT CLAIM. It does not claim scheduling isolation, hard
; cancellation, or that an entry is safe under all inputs: it measures entries
; and asserts the refusals it can observe. Cold compile is a dirty-CPU NIF call
; and the three cold samples are reported separately from the warm matrix; the
; port's handshake (spawn + IR parse + JIT) is likewise one separate sample. A
; fast wrong answer fails here rather than later: every measured batch's value
; is asserted, and the correctness matrix runs all 22 fixtures through every
; variant (the regular entry skipping the sizes it may not accept).
;
; ── RETURNED EVIDENCE (the exact schema) ────────────────────────────────────
;
;   {:passed        true            ; reached only if every assertion held
;    :checks        <int>           ; total assertions, all kinds
;    :check-counts  {kind <int> :total <int>}   ; :bench/:correctness/:refusal
;                                               ; /:cold/:warm/:stats
;    :api           {...}           ; the door names + the policy constants
;    :ir            {:path <str> :bytes <int>}
;    :rounds        <int>           ; 5
;    :variants      [<kw>…]         ; the measured doors, in declared order
;    :cold          [{:round :ns :probe-value :closed :ir-bytes}]
;    :cold-ns       [<int>]         ; the same, bare
;    :port-startup  {:exe <str> :ir <str> :ns <int>}   ; spawn → READY
;    :stats         {:before {…} :retained {…} :after {…}}   ; invm.host/stats
;    :stats-checks  {…}             ; the counter invariants actually asserted
;    :samples       [<sample>]      ; the timing matrix
;    :correctness   [<row>]         ; every (fixture, variant) value check
;    :refusals      [<row>]         ; every (input/handle, variant) refusal check
;    :matrix-refusals [<row>]       ; regular-NIF-large policy rows (no timing)
;    :summary       [<size-row>]    ; per size: 5 per-call samples + min/max/median
;    :counts        {…}             ; the matrix shape actually measured
;                                   ; (:correctness-rows includes the policy rows;
;                                   ;  :correctness-policy counts those)
;    :ns            {:bench <int>}  ; wall nanoseconds of the timing matrix
;    :limits        [<str>…]}       ; what was NOT shown, said plainly
;
;   <sample> {:variant :size :round :repeats :ns :inner-ns :value :expected
;             :reductions :memory-before :memory-after}
;   <row>    {:variant :tag :mode :size :value :expected :policy}
;            | {:variant :tag :mode :size :policy :cap}      ; matrix refusal
;   <size-row> {:size <int>
;               :variants {<kw> {:samples-ns [<int>] :per-call-ns [<int>]
;                                 :min-ns :max-ns :median-ns}
;                          | {:policy :refused-regular-cap-4096 :cap 4096
;                             :samples-ns [] :timing nil}}
;               :native-inner-median-ns <int>}   ; the port's own JIT scalar

(ns invm.bench)

;; ── constants ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(def REGULAR-CAP 4096)     ; the regular NIF entry's documented input cap
(def COLD-SAMPLES 3)       ; independent compile+close measurements
(def ROUNDS 5)             ; interleaved timing rounds per (fixture, variant)
(def MAX-REPEATS 200)      ; a call is repeated at most this many times
(def REPEAT-BUDGET 65536)  ; bytes·repeats budget: small inputs repeat more
(def VARIANTS [:rt :beam :port :nif :nif-dirty :noop :noop-dirty :bl-noop])
(def TALLY-KEY :invm-bench-checks)

;; ── assertions and the check tally ──────────────────────────────────────────
;;
;; Same shape as fusion.driver's tally: counted under a kind, and thrown on
;; every mismatch, with a non-boolean truthy value failing too.

(defn- reset-tally! []
  (erlang/put TALLY-KEY {})
  0)

(defn- tally! [kind]
  (let [counts (erlang/get TALLY-KEY)
        n (erlang/+ 1 (get counts kind 0))]
    (erlang/put TALLY-KEY (assoc counts kind n))
    n))

(defn- tally-count []
  (let [counts (erlang/get TALLY-KEY)]
    (assoc counts :total
           (reduce (fn [a k] (erlang/+ a (get counts k))) 0 (keys counts)))))

(defn- check!
  "A contract assertion — a value, a refusal, a counter invariant — counted
   under `kind` and thrown on every mismatch."
  [kind label ok]
  (tally! kind)
  (when (not (erlang/== true ok))
    (throw (ex-info (str "invm.bench: assertion failed: " label)
                    {:label label :kind kind :actual ok})))
  true)

;; ── clocks and process counters ─────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn- now [] (erlang/monotonic_time :nanosecond))
(defn- reductions [] (elem (erlang/process_info (erlang/self) :reductions) 1))
(defn- memory [] (elem (erlang/process_info (erlang/self) :memory) 1))

;; ── the doors ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn bl-noop
  "The pure-BL wrapper control: return `init` without touching `bin`. This is
   the harness floor, measured so the native entries are read against something
   that does no work at all."
  [bin init] init)

(defn- noop-variant?
  "True for the three entries that return the INITIAL accumulator, not the
   fold's result — their kernel output is different by construction."
  [v]
  (or (erlang/== v :noop) (erlang/== v :noop-dirty) (erlang/== v :bl-noop)))

(defn- runs?
  "Whether `variant` is admitted at `size`. The regular NIF entry caps at
   REGULAR-CAP bytes; every other door (and both no-ops, which never touch the
   buffer) admit the measured ladder."
  [variant size]
  (not (and (erlang/== variant :nif) (erlang/> size REGULAR-CAP))))

(defn- expected-for [variant f]
  (if (noop-variant? variant) (:initial f) (:expected f)))

(defn- call-variant
  "One call through one door, as {:value v :inner-ns n}. `inner-ns` is non-zero
   only for :port (the sidecar's own JIT scalar); the in-VM doors report 0 rather
   than inventing a timer. The binary is passed as-is on the native path — no
   conversion, and the resource is already compiled."
  [ctx variant f]
  (let [bin (:binary f) init (:initial f)]
    (cond
      (erlang/== variant :rt) {:value (fusion.pipeline/rt-run bin init) :inner-ns 0}
      (erlang/== variant :beam) {:value (fusion.pipeline/fused-run bin init) :inner-ns 0}
      (erlang/== variant :port)
        (let [r (fusion.driver/native-request! (:port ctx) init bin)]
          {:value (:value r) :inner-ns (:inner-ns r)})
      (erlang/== variant :nif)
        {:value (fusion.invm/kernel-call (:resource ctx) bin init) :inner-ns 0}
      (erlang/== variant :nif-dirty)
        {:value (fusion.invm/kernel-call-dirty (:resource ctx) bin init) :inner-ns 0}
      (erlang/== variant :noop)
        {:value (fusion.invm/kernel-noop bin init) :inner-ns 0}
      (erlang/== variant :noop-dirty)
        {:value (fusion.invm/kernel-noop-dirty bin init) :inner-ns 0}
      (erlang/== variant :bl-noop) {:value (bl-noop bin init) :inner-ns 0}
      :else (throw (ex-info (str "invm.bench: unknown variant " (pr-str variant)) {:variant variant})))))

;; ── cold compile: three independent compiles, each closed ───────────────────

(defn- cold-compile-samples
  "`COLD-SAMPLES` independent compiles of the SAME IR text, each timed alone,
   each used for exactly one empty-buffer call (proving the freshly compiled
   kernel answers and that this is the right fragment), then closed. The probe
   call is OUTSIDE the compile timer."
  [ir]
  (into []
    (map (fn [i]
           (let [t0 (now)
                 resource (fusion.invm/kernel-compile ir)
                 t1 (now)
                 probe (fusion.invm/kernel-call resource "" 0)
                 closed (fusion.invm/kernel-close resource)]
             (check! :cold (str "cold compile " i " answers an empty buffer with initial 0")
                     (erlang/== 0 probe))
             (check! :cold (str "cold compile " i " close returns true") (erlang/== true closed))
             {:round i :ns (erlang/- t1 t0) :ir-bytes (erlang/byte_size ir)
              :probe-value probe :closed closed}))
         (range COLD-SAMPLES))))

;; ── the timing matrix ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn- repeat-count
  "Repeats for a `size`-byte input: the byte budget divided by the size, floored
   at 1 (large inputs measured once) and capped at MAX-REPEATS (small inputs
   measured enough times to leave the clock's floor)."
  [size]
  (max 1 (min MAX-REPEATS (quot REPEAT-BUDGET (max 1 size)))))

(defn- rotate [v n]
  (let [k (erlang/rem n (count v))]
    (into [] (concat (drop k v) (take k v)))))

(defn- variant-order
  "Round `round`'s measurement order: rotate so each variant moves through every
   position across the five rounds, and reverse on odd rounds so no variant is
   always measured first OR always last. A warm/cold bias therefore lands on a
   different door each round."
  [round]
  (let [rot (rotate VARIANTS round)]
    (if (erlang/== 1 (erlang/rem round 2)) (into [] (reverse rot)) rot)))

(defn- measure-batch
  "Time `repeats` calls of one door over one fixture. Records the batch wall
   time, the summed native inner time (the port's own scalar), the reductions
   this process consumed, and its memory on both sides. The last call's value is
   kept; the caller asserts it against the oracle AFTER the timer stops, so the
   assertion never perturbs the measurement."
  [ctx variant f repeats]
  (erlang/garbage_collect)
  (let [m0 (memory)
        r0 (reductions)
        t0 (now)
        acc (loop [i 0 value nil inner 0]
              (if (erlang/== i repeats)
                {:value value :inner-ns inner}
                (let [r (call-variant ctx variant f)]
                  (recur (erlang/+ i 1) (:value r) (erlang/+ inner (:inner-ns r))))))
        t1 (now)]
    {:ns (erlang/- t1 t0)
     :value (:value acc)
     :inner-ns (:inner-ns acc)
     :reductions (erlang/- (reductions) r0)
     :memory-before m0
     :memory-after (memory)}))

(defn- bench-rows
  "The timing matrix: for every :bench fixture, one warm call per admitted
   variant, then ROUNDS interleaved batches per variant in the rotated order.
   Every batch's value is asserted against the fixture's expectation — a fast
   wrong answer fails here, not in a later pass."
  [ctx bench]
  (into []
    (mapcat
      (fn [f]
        (let [size (erlang/byte_size (:binary f))
              repeats (repeat-count size)]
          (doseq [v VARIANTS] (when (runs? v size) (call-variant ctx v f)))
          (into []
            (mapcat
              (fn [round]
                (into []
                  (mapcat
                    (fn [v]
                      (if (runs? v size)
                        (let [s (measure-batch ctx v f repeats)]
                          (check! :bench (str "bench value " (pr-str v) " size " size
                                              " round " round)
                                  (erlang/== (expected-for v f) (:value s)))
                          [(assoc s :variant v :size size :round round :repeats repeats
                                     :expected (expected-for v f))])
                        []))
                    (variant-order round))))
              (range ROUNDS)))))
      bench)))

;; ── correctness over every fixture, every admitted door ─────────────────────

(defn- correctness-rows
  "All 22 fixtures through every door, asserted against the oracle (the no-ops
   against the initial accumulator). The regular entry records a POLICY row for
   the sizes it may not accept instead of being silently absent."
  [ctx fixtures]
  (into []
    (mapcat
      (fn [f]
        (let [size (erlang/byte_size (:binary f))]
          (into []
            (mapcat
              (fn [v]
                (if (runs? v size)
                  (let [r (call-variant ctx v f)
                        want (expected-for v f)]
                    (check! :correctness (str "value " (pr-str v) " fixture " (:tag f))
                            (erlang/== want (:value r)))
                    [{:variant v :tag (:tag f) :mode (:mode f) :size size
                      :value (:value r) :expected want :policy :measured}])
                  [{:variant v :tag (:tag f) :mode (:mode f) :size size
                    :policy :refused-regular-cap-4096 :cap REGULAR-CAP}]))
              VARIANTS))))
      fixtures)))

;; ── the matrix's explicit policy refusals ───────────────────────────────────

(defn- policy-refusals
  "Regular-NIF rows for bench sizes above REGULAR-CAP: a refusal, never a zero."
  [bench]
  (into []
    (mapcat
      (fn [f]
        (let [size (erlang/byte_size (:binary f))]
          (if (erlang/> size REGULAR-CAP)
            [{:variant :nif :size size :cap REGULAR-CAP :policy :refused-regular-cap-4096
              :timing nil
              :reason (str "the regular NIF entry admits at most " REGULAR-CAP
                           " bytes; " size " bytes is a POLICY REFUSAL, not a zero-time sample")}]
            [])))
      bench)))

;; ── the refusals that are real calls ────────────────────────────────────────

(defn- refuses? [thunk]
  (try (do (thunk) false) (catch e true)))

(defn- refusal-rows
  "Invalid handles, invalid initial accumulators, oversized inputs, and the
   regular entry above its cap — each must THROW. A door that answers here is
   the failure. Every case is recorded with whether it refused."
  [ctx ir]
  (let [resource (:resource ctx)
        port (:port ctx)
        big (binary/copy (erlang/list_to_binary (list 0)) (erlang/+ fusion.fixtures/MAX-BYTES 1))
        over-regular (binary/copy (erlang/list_to_binary (list 0)) (erlang/+ REGULAR-CAP 1))
        closed (let [r (fusion.invm/kernel-compile ir)]
                 (fusion.invm/kernel-close r)
                 r)
        cases
        [{:case "handle-closed" :variant :nif
          :call (fn [] (fusion.invm/kernel-call closed "" 0))}
         {:case "handle-forged-binary" :variant :nif
          :call (fn [] (fusion.invm/kernel-call "not-a-resource" "" 0))}
         {:case "handle-forged-integer" :variant :nif-dirty
          :call (fn [] (fusion.invm/kernel-call-dirty 42 "" 0))}
         {:case "buffer-nonbinary" :variant :nif
          :call (fn [] (fusion.invm/kernel-call resource :not-a-binary 0))}
         {:case "init-float" :variant :nif
          :call (fn [] (fusion.invm/kernel-call resource "" 1.5))}
         {:case "init-negative" :variant :nif
          :call (fn [] (fusion.invm/kernel-call resource "" -1))}
         {:case "init>u64" :variant :nif
          :call (fn [] (fusion.invm/kernel-call resource "" (erlang/+ fusion.fixtures/U64 1)))}
         {:case "init-noninteger" :variant :nif
          :call (fn [] (fusion.invm/kernel-call resource "" "0"))}
         {:case "buffer>regular-cap" :variant :nif
          :call (fn [] (fusion.invm/kernel-call resource over-regular 0))}
         {:case "buffer>1MiB" :variant :nif-dirty
          :call (fn [] (fusion.invm/kernel-call-dirty resource big 0))}
         {:case "noop-buffer>1MiB" :variant :noop
          :call (fn [] (fusion.invm/kernel-noop big 0))}
         {:case "noop-dirty-init-negative" :variant :noop-dirty
          :call (fn [] (fusion.invm/kernel-noop-dirty "" -1))}
         {:case "port-buffer>1MiB" :variant :port
          :call (fn [] (fusion.driver/native-request! port 0 big))}
         {:case "port-init-negative" :variant :port
          :call (fn [] (fusion.driver/native-request! port -1 ""))}
         {:case "rt-buffer>1MiB" :variant :rt
          :call (fn [] (fusion.pipeline/rt-run big 0))}
         {:case "beam-buffer>1MiB" :variant :beam
          :call (fn [] (fusion.pipeline/fused-run big 0))}]
        rows
        (mapv (fn [c]
                (let [threw (refuses? (:call c))]
                  (check! :refusal (str "refusal " (:variant c) " " (:case c)) threw)
                  {:variant (:variant c) :case (:case c) :refused threw}))
              cases)]
    {:rows rows
     :refused (count (filterv (fn [r] (erlang/== true (:refused r))) rows))
     :total (count rows)}))

;; ── aggregation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn- median [xs]
  (let [ordered (into [] (sort xs))]
    (nth ordered (quot (count ordered) 2))))

(defn- per-call-ns [samples size variant]
  (into []
    (map (fn [s] (quot (:ns s) (:repeats s)))
         (filterv (fn [s] (and (erlang/== size (:size s))
                               (erlang/== variant (:variant s))))
                  samples))))

(defn- per-call-inner [samples size]
  (into []
    (map (fn [s] (quot (:inner-ns s) (:repeats s)))
         (filterv (fn [s] (and (erlang/== size (:size s))
                               (erlang/== :port (:variant s))))
                  samples))))

(defn- stats-for [acc]
  (if (empty? acc)
    {:samples-ns [] :per-call-ns [] :timing nil :policy :not-measured
     :min-ns nil :max-ns nil :median-ns nil}
    {:samples-ns acc :per-call-ns acc :timing :measured :policy :measured
     :min-ns (reduce min acc) :max-ns (reduce max acc) :median-ns (median acc)}))

(defn- summarize
  "Per bench size: the five per-call samples and their min/max/median for each
   door, or the explicit POLICY row when the regular entry may not be called.
   Exposed as data so a caller can re-derive anything the printed table drops."
  [samples bench]
  (mapv
    (fn [f]
      (let [size (erlang/byte_size (:binary f))]
        {:size size
         :variants
           (into {}
             (map (fn [v]
                    [v (if (runs? v size)
                         (stats-for (per-call-ns samples size v))
                         {:policy :refused-regular-cap-4096 :cap REGULAR-CAP
                          :samples-ns [] :per-call-ns [] :timing nil
                          :min-ns nil :max-ns nil :median-ns nil})])
                  VARIANTS))
         :native-inner-median-ns (let [xs (per-call-inner samples size)]
                                   (if (empty? xs) nil (median xs)))}))
    bench))

;; ── the human table (from captured data — no rerun) ─────────────────────────

(defn- us [v] (if (nil? v) "refused" (/ v 1000.0)))

(defn- print-table [summary cold port-startup refusals]
  (println "bytes | rt us | beam us | port us | nif us | nif-dirty us | noop us | noop-dirty us | bl-noop us | regular")
  (doseq [row summary]
    (let [vs (:variants row)
          m (fn [v] (:median-ns (get vs v)))]
      (println (str (:size row)
                    " | " (us (m :rt))
                    " | " (us (m :beam))
                    " | " (us (m :port))
                    " | " (us (m :nif))
                    " | " (us (m :nif-dirty))
                    " | " (us (m :noop))
                    " | " (us (m :noop-dirty))
                    " | " (us (m :bl-noop))
                    " | " (let [entry (get vs :nif)]
                            (if (erlang/== :refused-regular-cap-4096 (:policy entry))
                              "refused"
                              "measured"))))))
  (println (str "cold-compile-ns=" (pr-str (mapv (fn [c] (:ns c)) cold))))
  (println (str "port-startup-ns=" (:ns port-startup)))
  (println (str "input-refusals=" (:refused refusals) "/" (:total refusals))))

;; ── the diagnostics shape ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn- stats-shape!
  "The ONE shape this file accepts from invm.host/stats — the normalized map
   {:created :live :freed :inflight}. Asserted, not pattern-matched, so an
   unnormalized counter tuple fails by name instead of turning into arithmetic
   on nil."
  [s]
  (check! :stats "invm.host/stats returns the normalized {:created :live :freed :inflight} map"
          (and (erlang/is_map s)
               (contains? s :created) (contains? s :live)
               (contains? s :freed) (contains? s :inflight)))
  s)

;; ── the entry point ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn run
  "Measure every door over the shared fixtures and return the evidence map
   described at the top of this file. Reads the IR text ONCE; the port is
   spawned once and closed in a `finally`; the retained NIF resource is closed
   in a `finally` even when the port half fails. No exception is swallowed."
  [port-exe ir-path]
  (reset-tally!)
  (let [ir (File/read! ir-path)
        stats-before (stats-shape! (invm.host/stats))
        cold (cold-compile-samples ir)
        resource (fusion.invm/kernel-compile ir)
        stats-retained (stats-shape! (invm.host/stats))
        body
          (try
            (let [t0 (now)
                  port (fusion.driver/spawn-fold! port-exe ir-path)
                  measured
                    (try
                      (fusion.driver/await-ready! port)
                      (let [port-ns (erlang/- (now) t0)
                            ctx {:resource resource :port port}
                            warm (fusion.invm/kernel-call resource "" 0)
                            fixtures (fusion.fixtures/make)
                            bench (fusion.fixtures/bench-fixtures)
                            correctness (correctness-rows ctx fixtures)
                            samples (bench-rows ctx bench)
                            refusals (refusal-rows ctx ir)
                            policy (policy-refusals bench)
                            summary (summarize samples bench)]
                        (check! :warm "the retained kernel answers an empty buffer with initial 0"
                                (erlang/== 0 warm))
                        {:port-ns port-ns :warm warm :fixtures fixtures :bench bench
                         :correctness correctness :samples samples :refusals refusals
                         :policy policy :summary summary})
                      (finally (Port/close port)))]
              measured)
            (finally (fusion.invm/kernel-close resource)))
        stats-after (stats-shape! (invm.host/stats))
        stats-checks
          {:before-inflight-zero (erlang/== 0 (:inflight stats-before))
           :retained-inflight-zero (erlang/== 0 (:inflight stats-retained))
           :after-inflight-zero (erlang/== 0 (:inflight stats-after))
           :live-restored (erlang/== (:live stats-before) (:live stats-after))
           :created-delta (erlang/- (:created stats-after) (:created stats-before))
           :freed-delta (erlang/- (:freed stats-after) (:freed stats-before))}
        _ (check! :stats "no call is in flight before the run" (:before-inflight-zero stats-checks))
        _ (check! :stats "no call is in flight while the resource is retained"
                  (:retained-inflight-zero stats-checks))
        _ (check! :stats "no call is in flight after every resource is closed"
                  (:after-inflight-zero stats-checks))
        _ (check! :stats "the live count returns to its starting value"
                  (:live-restored stats-checks))
        _ (check! :stats "every created kernel is actually freed"
                  (and (>= (:created-delta stats-checks) (erlang/+ COLD-SAMPLES 1))
                       (erlang/== (:freed-delta stats-checks) (:created-delta stats-checks))))
        samples (:samples body)
        tally (tally-count)
        bench-ns (reduce (fn [a s] (erlang/+ a (:ns s))) 0 samples)
        result
          {:passed true
           :checks (:total tally)
           :check-counts tally
           :api {:variants VARIANTS
                 :regular-cap REGULAR-CAP
                 :max-bytes fusion.fixtures/MAX-BYTES
                 :entries {:rt "fusion.pipeline/rt-run"
                           :beam "fusion.pipeline/fused-run"
                           :port "fusion.driver/native-request!"
                           :nif "fusion.invm/kernel-call"
                           :nif-dirty "fusion.invm/kernel-call-dirty"
                           :noop "fusion.invm/kernel-noop"
                           :noop-dirty "fusion.invm/kernel-noop-dirty"
                           :bl-noop "invm.bench/bl-noop"}}
           :ir {:path ir-path :bytes (erlang/byte_size ir)}
           :rounds ROUNDS
           :variants VARIANTS
           :cold cold
           :cold-ns (into [] (map (fn [c] (:ns c)) cold))
           :port-startup {:exe port-exe :ir ir-path :ns (:port-ns body)}
           :stats {:before stats-before :retained stats-retained :after stats-after}
           :stats-checks stats-checks
           :samples samples
           :correctness (:correctness body)
           :refusals (:refusals body)
           :matrix-refusals (:policy body)
           :summary (:summary body)
           :counts {:fixtures (count (:fixtures body))
                    :bench-fixtures (count (:bench body))
                    :variants (count VARIANTS)
                    :rounds ROUNDS
                    :cold-samples COLD-SAMPLES
                    :samples (count samples)
                    :correctness-rows (count (:correctness body))
                    :correctness-policy (count (filterv (fn [r] (erlang/== :refused-regular-cap-4096 (:policy r)))
                                                        (:correctness body)))
                    :refusal-cases (:total (:refusals body))
                    :matrix-refusals (count (:policy body))
                    :regular-cap REGULAR-CAP}
           :ns {:bench bench-ns}
           :limits ["Cold compile and the port handshake are measured separately from the warm matrix."
                    "The regular NIF entry above 4096 bytes is a POLICY REFUSAL with no timing — never a zero."
                    "Scheduling isolation, hard cancellation and crash isolation are NOT measured here."
                    "The pure-BL :bl-noop row is the harness floor, not a kernel."]}
        _ (print-table (:summary body) cold (:port-startup result) (:refusals body))]
    (println (str "PASS invm bench: checks=" (:checks result)
                  " samples=" (count samples)
                  " cold-ns=" (pr-str (:cold-ns result))
                  " port-startup-ns=" (:ns (:port-startup result))
                  " refusals=" (:refused (:refusals body)) "/" (:total (:refusals body))
                  " matrix-refusals=" (count (:policy body))))
    result))
